@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy"; }
<header class="page-header"><div class="page-header-copy"><span class="eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION</span><h1>Privacy at FitTrack</h1><p>A plain-language overview of the information FitTrack uses to provide its features.</p></div></header>
<div class="privacy-content">
    <section class="app-card mb-3"><h2 class="h5">Information stored in FitTrack</h2><p>FitTrack stores your account details, fitness profile, workout plans, workout history, and progress measurements in the application’s configured database. Profile photos you add are stored with the application’s uploaded files.</p></section>
    <section class="app-card mb-3"><h2 class="h5">Optional AI coach</h2><p>If you use the AI coach or generate an AI plan, FitTrack sends your question or plan request along with relevant profile and recent training information to the AI provider configured by the application owner. AI features are optional; you can use the workout planner, history, and progress features without them.</p></section>
    <section class="app-card"><h2 class="h5">Exercise catalog</h2><p>The exercise library retrieves catalog information from wger and keeps a temporary application cache so it can continue to show a recent copy during a short outage.</p></section>
</div>
